Recipe, spec, workflow


Show code
rf_recipe &lt;- make_recipe(train)

# 1000 trees fixed (more is just slower, not better once stable); tune mtry and
# min_n. importance = "permutation" so we can plot variable importance.
rf_spec &lt;- rand_forest(
  mtry  = tune(),
  min_n = tune(),
  trees = 1000
) |&gt;
  set_engine("ranger", importance = "permutation") |&gt;
  set_mode("regression")

rf_wf &lt;- workflow() |&gt;
  add_recipe(rf_recipe) |&gt;
  add_model(rf_spec)

The workflow
A workflow bundles the recipe and the model so resampling applies the exact same preprocessing to every fold — no leakage.


Show code
xgb_wf &lt;- workflow() |&gt;
  add_recipe(xgb_recipe) |&gt;
  add_model(xgb_spec)

Recipe, spec, workflow
The shared recipe already normalizes all numeric predictors and appends PCs, so the MLP sees well-behaved inputs. We tune the hidden-layer width and the weight decay penalty, and lean on num_comp to control input dimensionality.


Show code
nnet_recipe &lt;- make_recipe(train)

nnet_spec &lt;- mlp(
  hidden_units = tune(),
  penalty      = tune(),
  epochs       = 300
) |&gt;
  # MaxNWts must be large enough for (many predictors) x (hidden units); trace
  # off to keep the tuning log quiet. linout is set automatically in regression.
  set_engine("nnet", MaxNWts = 10000, trace = FALSE) |&gt;
  set_mode("regression")

nnet_wf &lt;- workflow() |&gt;
  add_recipe(nnet_recipe) |&gt;
  add_model(nnet_spec)

